course: dictionary
lesson: 9579
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around it. In «A combine harvester cuts the wheat, beats out the grains and blows away the straw at once», the straw is the part left after the grain is taken. Dry stalks are the only thing that could be blown away, so straw means dry stalks here.
explain: Now look at «An adult elephant can hold about 8 litres of water in its trunk and then blows it into its mouth; it does not drink through it like a straw.» The clue is «drink through it». So a straw is a thin tube you drink through, and the elephant does not do that.
explain: Some phrases have a meaning that is not the same as the words. «The last straw» is a small problem that makes you lose your patience, even though it is not really a straw at all. When you meet a phrase that does not make sense word by word, try the meaning that fits the sentence, then check it in a dictionary if you are not sure.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: The same word can have different meanings: straw can be dry stalks, a thin drinking tube, or a phrase like «the last straw».
fact: «Straw» (noun) means the dry yellow stalks of plants like wheat, used for animal beds or to make hats and baskets.
fact: «Draw straws» means to choose by picking from straws of different lengths, and the one who gets the short straw is chosen.
fact: Plastic straws can harm sea life, so people use paper or reusable ones instead.

exercise: «A combine harvester cuts the wheat, beats out the grains and blows away the straw at once.» What is the straw in this sentence? | A hat made by a weaver | A small problem that makes you lose patience | A thin tube for drinking | * The dry yellow stalks left after the grain is taken
exercise: «An adult elephant ... does not drink through it like a straw.» What is a straw used for? | Choosing by picking from lengths | * A thin tube for drinking | Blowing water into your mouth | Dry stalks for animal beds
exercise: Which phrase means the last small problem that makes you lose patience? | draw straws | a straw-like mouth | a house of straw | * the last straw

test: Draw straws means | To sip a drink very quickly | * To choose by picking from straws of different lengths | To sweep the dry stalks off the barn floor | To draw pictures with a drinking straw
test: In the story, the three little pigs built a house of what? | bricks | stone | * straw | sticks

exam: Plastic straws harm sea life, so which choice is better? | * Paper or reusable straws | Straw bales left on the beach | More plastic cups | Plastic straws in bigger packs
